    {
      "id": "20002036",
      "title": "Sub-Networks",
      "subtitle": "Channel-Efficient Subnet Design",
      "description": [
        "A sub-network is a separate AE2 network that accesses your main network storage but uses its own channel budget.",
        "Design: Storage Bus on the sub-network's cable (different color) pointed at an ME Interface on the main network",
        "The sub-network sees everything in main storage but all its devices consume channels from the sub-network's Controller, not the main one",
        "Use for dedicated autocrafting clusters that would otherwise drain all 32 channels from your main Controller face.",
        "Tip: Give your sub-network a dedicated Controller with its own power supply. A single Crystal Resonance Generator powers a small sub-network indefinitely from certus quartz."
      ],
      "icon": "ae2:storage_bus",
